LIGGGHTS (Version LIGGGHTS-PUBLIC 3.8.0, compiled 2026-11-11 09:50:45 by su_estupinan, git commit b0596d1b6dca30fe03789ecd9b3e0112edc1d23d, build configuration: MPI VTK SURROGATE SMALLBIG, models: HERTZ TANGENTIAL_HISTORY TANGENTIAL_NO_HISTORY COHESION_SJKR COHESION_SJKR2 ROLLING_EPSD2 SURFACE_DEFAULT)
# Test Case 01: Surrogate Contact - Cube (L=1m) Falling on Plane
#
# Purpose: Test surrogate contact model with trained characteristic length (L=1m)
# Expected: Cube should fall, contact with plane via surrogate model, bounce back
#
# Model: run_029 (ss-cube-walls, 84.7% accuracy)
# Shape: ss-cube with L_actual = 1.0 m (matches training scale)
#
# Physics:
# - Hertz contact + tangential history
# - Density: 1000 kg/m³ (water-like, for stability)
# - No cohesion or rolling friction (simple case)

# ===== Simulation Control =====
units           si
atom_style      surrogate ss-cube
dimension       3
boundary        f f f

# Pair style gran with shear history requires newton off
newton          off

# ===== Geometry =====
region          domain block -5.0 5.0 -5.0 5.0 0.0 20.0 units box
create_box      1 domain
Created orthogonal box = (-5 -5 0) to (5 5 20)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid

# ===== Particle Creation =====
# Single cube particle at height z=10m, falling under gravity
# Characteristic length L = 1.0 m (trained model size)
create_atoms    1 single 0.0 0.0 10.0
Created 1 atoms

# ===== Material Properties =====
# Density: 1000 kg/m³
# Mass = density * volume = 1000 * 1³ = 1000 kg
# For sphere-like particles, use 'set' command instead of 'mass'
set             atom * mass 1000.0
  1 settings made for mass

# Set characteristic length (for surrogate particles)
# This MUST match the trained model scale
set             atom * diameter 1.0
  1 settings made for diameter

# ===== Material Properties - Hertz Contact =====
# Define material properties required by Hertz contact model
fix             materialproperties all property/global youngsModulus peratomtype 1.0e9
fix             materialproperties2 all property/global poissonsRatio peratomtype 0.25
fix             materialproperties3 all property/global coefficientRestitution peratomtypepair 1 0.9
fix             materialproperties4 all property/global coefficientFriction peratomtypepair 1 0.2

# ===== Velocity & Forces =====
# Initial velocity: 0 (free fall)
velocity        all set 0.0 0.0 0.0

# NVE integration (Newtonian Velocity Verlet Ensemble)
# Applies Newton's laws of motion to surrogate particles
fix             integrate all nve/sphere

# Gravity: 9.81 m/s² downward
fix             gravity all gravity 9.81 vector 0.0 0.0 -1.0

# ===== Wall (Primitive Plane) =====
# Plane wall at z=0, facing upward (normal = +z)
# Syntax: wall/gran model hertz tangential history primitive type 1 zplane z_coord
fix             wall all wall/gran model hertz tangential history primitive type 1 zplane 0.0
WARNING: 
	The contact model you specified is not located in any whitelist.
	Because of this the model will be run in an unoptimized version (increasing runtime by up to 20%).
	In order to optimize this model you have the following options:
		(i)  Run the genAutoExamplesWhitelist.sh script in your LIGGGHTS(R) source folder to automatically parse the input script
		(ii) Add the model combination by hand to your style_contact_model_user.whitelist that can be found in your LIGGGHTS(R) source folder
		(iii) Use the ENABLE_MODEL_* flag when building with cmake.
	If you perform one of the steps above LIGGGHTS(R) needs to be recompiled to generate the optimized code.

 (/home/su_estupinan@private.list.lu/SpaceLights/LIGGGHTS-PUBLIC/src/contact_models.h:365)

# ===== Contact Model =====
# For surrogate particles with wall contact only (Phase 3C):
# Wall/gran fix handles all contact via surrogate model
# Pair style gran is used for neighbor list building only (no particle-particle contacts in this test)

pair_style      gran model hertz tangential history
WARNING: 
	The contact model you specified is not located in any whitelist.
	Because of this the model will be run in an unoptimized version (increasing runtime by up to 20%).
	In order to optimize this model you have the following options:
		(i)  Run the genAutoExamplesWhitelist.sh script in your LIGGGHTS(R) source folder to automatically parse the input script
		(ii) Add the model combination by hand to your style_contact_model_user.whitelist that can be found in your LIGGGHTS(R) source folder
		(iii) Use the ENABLE_MODEL_* flag when building with cmake.
	If you perform one of the steps above LIGGGHTS(R) needs to be recompiled to generate the optimized code.

 (/home/su_estupinan@private.list.lu/SpaceLights/LIGGGHTS-PUBLIC/src/contact_models.h:365)

# Define minimal pair coefficients (required for pair_style gran)
pair_coeff      * *

# Disable atom sorting (not needed for single particle)
neigh_modify    check no delay 0

# ===== Time Integration =====
timestep        0.0001

# Compute kinetic and potential energy (must come before thermo_style)
compute         thermo_kinetic all ke
compute         thermo_potential all pe

thermo          100
thermo_style    custom step atoms c_thermo_kinetic c_thermo_potential

# ===== Run =====
# Simulate for 2 seconds (20,000 timesteps at dt=0.0001)
run             20000
